{
  "schema": "https://chriopter.github.io/pspdx/schema/pspdx-v1.json",
  "source": "https://github.com/chriopter/pspkit-usbnet",
  "name": "USBNet",
  "type": "plugin",
  "category": "plugin",
  "tags": [
    "network",
    "usb"
  ],
  "summary": "Bring your PSP online over the USB cable.",
  "author": "chriopter",
  "license": "MIT",
  "description": "Up to ten times faster than Wi-Fi, in all apps and games.\n\nYou need to run the gateway on your PC. Get it at github.com/chriopter/pspkit-usbnet\n\nNeeds ARK custom firmware. After installing, restart the PSP.\n\nOnce, create the connection: Network Settings > Infrastructure Mode > New Connection > Scan > \"Hi-Speed USB\" > Security: None > save. Then connect with \"Hi-Speed USB\", like with Wi-Fi, while the gateway runs.\n\nHold START at power-on to start the PSP without plugins."
}
